Subject: [PATCH 67/68] MOSIP's screens with Noto Sans at 360 dp: three texts
 no longer cut off, and a layout test (task 30)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The app-wide Noto Sans (task 21) was layout-tested only on the liveness screens. mosip_screens_layout_test pumps
MOSIP's own screens with the app's theme, its ScreenUtil set-up and the bundled fonts at 360x740 dp, at text
scales 1.0 and 1.3, in English, French and Hindi. It fails on any overflow (or other error while building) and on any
text cut off at its line limit. There is no backend: the providers' start-up loads are switched off in test
subclasses, and the screens get a synced client's state (languages, a dashboard with counts and three operators,
placeholder names). A self-check proves both detectors fire.

Covered:
- sign-in (username and password steps);
- home: operational tasks, and the dashboard, settings and profile tabs;
- the supervisor's approval page;
- operator onboarding.
Not built:
- the registration flow, which needs the server's process spec;
- the export page, which creates its own provider and loads packets natively;
- OnboardLandingPage, a registered route nothing navigates to, with no Scaffold of its own.

Found and fixed (minimal; each failed the test first):
- The bottom navigation labels: "Dashboard" at 1.3, French "Tableau de bord" at 1.0 and 1.3, and "Paramètres" at 1.3
  were cut to "…" (62 dp available; natural widths 69, 77, 100 and 72 dp).
  - The tile's horizontal padding is 4 dp instead of 14 on phones, which leaves 82 dp.
  - A label still too wide shrinks to fit (FittedBox, scaleDown): French at 1.3.
- The dashboard's "Active - Not Onboarded" status (English included, at 1.0) and "inactive" were ellipsized in their
  table column. They wrap now, and the row grows.
- The approval page's title, "Pending Approval" at 1.3 and French, shrinks to fit instead of ending in "…".

Known, not changed: the approval search field's floating label ("Search by Application ID") is cut on a 360 dp
phone, English at 1.0 included. That is MOSIP's layout (two thirds of the row beside the submit button) and needs a
layout change. The test names it as a known exception.

flutter test test/liveness: 339 passing (330 + 9), 20 skipped.

